{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/342717-around-the-world-in-a-hundred-years-talk-about-the-weather-open-dev","id":342717,"title":"Around the World in A Hundred Years - Talk About The Weather (Open Dev)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-17T01:24:16-08:00","id":342717,"title":"Around the World in A Hundred Years - Talk About The Weather (Open Dev)","content":"So, for those who don't keep up with the blog posts, the Firestorm Chronicle Anthology's <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/anthology-ahoy/\" target=\"_blank\">done with editing</a>, which means we get a wonderful look at Wood's piece for the End section. My highlights:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Reinforcing/driving home the sheer <i>scale</i> of Crow's existence - it's one thing to read that the old bird's flown around the world multiple times in the Magnum Opus writeup and an entirely different matter to hear exemplary snippets of the kind of sheer <i>lore</i> that's grown up around a talking crow with a collection of stories about <i>every Promethean he's ever known of.</i><br /> \u2022 Relatedly, drawing upon the rarity and strikingness of the Created as beings that almost can't <i>help</i> but spawn folk tales and urban legends.<br /> \u2022 Vanishing glass mansions, omens in the quick glimpse of a pack of werewolves, and what I strongly suspect to be a Frances Black cameo all lending to the atmosphere of the WoD as a place of plentiful strangeness.<br /> \u2022 Windscale's Carcinomas providing an example of Pandorans doing things other than be hungry and physically vicious - in retrospect, this seems like the stuff Fever Dreams was devised for.<br /> \u2022 Israel's &quot;vivid imagination.&quot;<br /> <br /> Share your own or discuss the anthology in general; y'all know how these threads work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T03:26:15-08:00","id":342758,"title":"","content":"Well, you summed it up quite nicely. I think I also caught a reference to the the Chevalier Theleme during Israel and Sister Stich's travels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T21:58:16-08:00","id":343675,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly just pleased to see so many old favorites come back. I can honestly say that I thought we'd heart the last of Israel Hands and Hendaid Bran. This excerpt won me over on buying the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T05:39:48-08:00","id":343813,"title":"","content":"None of the other stories reference characters from 1E, I don't think, but I really wanted Wood to contribute a story precisely so we could see some of these folks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T20:39:44-08:00","id":352287,"title":"","content":"Do we have a rough estimate on when we can get our grubby paws on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T09:47:22-08:00","id":355821,"title":"","content":"It was supposed to go up for sale last week and apparently there was some kind of technical glitch. My understanding is it should be up this week (or next; holiday).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:58:18-08:00","id":356642,"title":"","content":"It is already out. Just finished the Zeka story. So very beautiful.<br /> What were those raven things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T23:30:50-08:00","id":358073,"title":"","content":"I threw a <a href=\"http://www.drivethrufiction.com/product_reviews.php?products_id=141741\" target=\"_blank\">review</a> up, if anyone's curious; gave it a 4/5. I'm pleased with the book as a whole, though the decision to put the collection's few duds at the very front of the anthology nearly scared me away. As the poster above me said, <i>Beautiful Strange</i> is one of the highlights of the entire thing, along with <i>Some Running Night</i> and <i>Talk About The Weather</i>. I'm not ashamed to admit that I cried, though I won't say which story did me in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I managed to forget to mention <i>To Each Her Adam</i> entirely, but it was one of the more average tales in the anthology. Oops!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}